messages.content:
Modelica source:
```modelica
connector Pin
  Real v;
  flow Real i;
end Pin;
model TwoPin
  Pin p;
  Pin n;
end TwoPin;
model Ground
  Pin p;
end Ground;
model MOS
  Pin S;
  Pin D;
  Pin B;
  Pin G;
end MOS;
model Study
  TwoPin Sin;
  TwoPin V;
  TwoPin Capacitor1;
  MOS H_PMOS;
  MOS H_NMOS;
  Ground G;
equation
  connect(Sin.n, G.p);
  connect(Capacitor1.n, G.p);
  connect(H_PMOS.S, H_NMOS.D);
  connect(H_NMOS.D, Capacitor1.p);
  connect(H_NMOS.B, H_NMOS.S);
  connect(H_NMOS.S, G.p);
  connect(H_PMOS.B, H_PMOS.D);
  connect(V.p, H_PMOS.D);
  connect(V.n, G.p);
  connect(H_NMOS.G, Sin.p);
  connect(H_PMOS.G, Sin.p);
end Study;
```

Question:
Are Sin.p.v,V.p.v in the same primitive potential connection set? Return true or false.

Target:
Sin.p.v,V.p.v

Answer format:
Use exactly true or false in the answer string.
